message: "If you use this record, please cite it as below."
title: "Coding agent hosting benchmark: which platform Claude Code commits to, season by season"
authors:
  - family-names: Grande
    given-names: Alberto
date-released: 2026-11-18
version: "2.0.0"
license: CC-BY-4.0
url: "https://thebeat.dev/research/how-claude-code-picks-a-host/"
abstract: >-
  Which hosting platform Claude Code picks for a real app, and what decides it.
  1,133 runs of 11 apps under one-line briefs, on Opus 5 and Opus 5.5. A line in
  the repo that names a host moved 96 of 99 picks to it. With nothing in the repo
  about hosting, the agent picked from what its model already knows in a quarter
  to a half of runs, and when it went online it mostly read the docs of the host it
  then picked. The record holds every run, every label, the grader and the harness.
keywords:
  - answer engine optimization
  - AEO
